Z||000000||wxxo||03-15-2000||05:02 PM||||what should an air filter look like when it needs to be replaced. mine looks pretty good but man am i getting bad gas mileage. just got it out of the shop and 300 bucks later it still isnt any better. what else could be causing the poor gas mileage. by the way i already checked...no hole in the gas tank haha. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||03-15-2000||05:11 PM||||If this is a V6 the air flows from the inside to the outside. It can look great on the outside an be filthy inside.<P>If you are in doubt, I would buy one. When you change it hold the old and new one up to a bright light to get a "baseline" of what a clean one looks like.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wxxo||03-15-2000||06:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>If this is a V6 the air flows from the inside to the outside. It can look great on the outside an be filthy inside.<P>If you are in doubt, I would buy one. When you change it hold the old and new one up to a bright light to get a "baseline" of what a clean one looks like.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>ill do that. thanks. are there any that will boost performance??<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-15-2000||08:01 PM||||I usually hold the filter up to a light and see how much illumination shows through the filter. If it looks bright, the filter's ok. If hardly any light shows through, replace it.||||reg||1
